  </header>

  <div class="note-body reading-width">
    <section class="update-card" data-route="browser" hidden>
      <h2>Update it right here <span class="beta">Beta</span></h2>
      <ol class="update-steps">
        <li>Plug the card's DATA port into this <span data-device>computer</span>.</li>
        <li>Hold BOOT, plug a charger into POWER, then let go. The display stays off.</li>
        <li>Press Update and pick your card.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="update-aside" data-linux-help hidden>First time on Linux? Chrome needs a udev rule, its under <a href="#trouble" data-open-trouble>Trouble</a>.</p>
      <button class="update-button" type="button" data-update>Update</button>
      <div class="update-progress" data-progress hidden>
        <progress max="100" value="0"></progress>
        <p><span data-status>Getting the firmware…</span> Keep the card plugged in.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="update-result" data-result role="status" hidden></p>
    </section>

